# Twelve loops stand inside one another and each grows a text of its own, so each wants a second walk, for its text in a builder. A loop that has loops inside it tells the walk
# around it what it wants, and that walk is walked again: once for the texts, and once more because every loop is then found to run no other code: four walks a level; the innermost loop alone meets its wish at once: two walks more. Where every level met its wish at once, each level walked itself and all inside it again: 103 walks
